Package: ds212j-support
Version: 1.8
Architecture: all
Maintainer: lepirlouit <bdb@aloalto.com>
Depends: mdadm, systemd, util-linux, smartmontools, hdparm, python3, ethtool
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Description: Synology DS-212j board support (LEDs, buzzer) for Debian
 Reproduces the DSM LED and buzzer behaviour on a Synology DS-212j running
 Debian with a mainline kernel:
  - power LED blinking while booting/shutting down, steady when up, and one
    beep when boot has finished (microcontroller on UART1);
  - STATUS LED green when all md arrays are healthy, blinking orange when one
    is degraded or missing;
  - amber HDD LEDs on when a disk is faulty in an md array or fails SMART;
  - front LAN LED working at 1000 Mb/s too (Ethernet PHY LED configuration);
  - DSM fan modes (full, cool, quiet, low-power) driven by the hottest disk
    temperature, including the 61 C emergency shutdown;
  - DSM disk hibernation: spin-down delay (10 min by default), journal kept
    in RAM and saved to disk daily and at shutdown, and while the disks sleep
    only the power LED stays lit and the fan stops.
  - network that keeps working under memory pressure: no scatter-gather/TSO
    on eth0 and a larger free-memory reserve.
